1) docker build command :
- Syntax : docker build [OPTIONS] PATH | URL
PATH - The build context - usually the working directory

- ex : docker build -t myapp .

- by default, docker looks for a file named Dockerfile, but you can specify different name also.

2) Docker build command for the different file name and build copntext path

- ex : docker build -f /path/test.txt -t image3 /imagefile
    - Build the image image3 from the test.txt file 
    - The /imagefile is build context
